intent: PR #93 CI: Windows fails learning pipeline checks because they spawn bin.js from a file URL pathname (C:\D:\...), and CodeQL flags incomplete regex escaping in the new version-consistency test. Use fileURLToPath for the CLI path and a string-based heading check; test-only changes.
criteria:
- windows-cli-path: tests/learning/pipeline-checks.mjs spawns the compiled CLI with fileURLToPath instead of a file URL pathname, so learning-cli-history-reconciliation and learning-compatibility-delivery no longer fail with MODULE_NOT_FOUND 'C:\D:\...\bin.js' on Windows; node-test passes.
- codeql-heading-check: tests/release/version-consistency.test.ts checks for a dated `## [<version>] - YYYY-MM-DD` heading below `## [Unreleased]` without building a regular expression from the version string (removing the CodeQL incomplete-escaping alert) while still failing when the heading is missing or above Unreleased; node-test passes.
